{"name":"Plymouth Notch","hex":"#cdb3ac","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"notch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A V-shaped cut.\nSuch a cut, used for keeping a record.","Such a cut, used for keeping a record."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cut a notch in (something).","To record (a score or similar) by making notches on something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plymouth Notch, Vermont","blocks":[{"text":"Plymouth Notch is an unincorporated community in the town of Plymouth, Windsor County, Vermont, United States. All or most of the village is included in the Calvin Coolidge Homestead District, a National Historic Landmark."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Plymouth_Notch_Vermont_USA_birthplace_of_Calvin_Coolidge.JPG/330px-Plymouth_Notch_Vermont_USA_birthplace_of_Calvin_Coolidge.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plymouth_Notch%2C_Vermont","wikidata":"Q7205837"},{"title":"Plymouth","blocks":[{"text":"Plymouth is a port city and unitary authority in Devon, England. It is located on the county's south coast between the rivers Plym and Tamar, about 36 miles (58 km) south-west of Exeter and 193 miles (311 km) south-west of London. It is the most populous settlement in Devon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Plymouth_City.JPG/330px-Plymouth_City.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plymouth","wikidata":"Q43382"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Plymouth_Barbican_2022.jpg/500px-Plymouth_Barbican_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Plymouth_Barbican_2022.jpg/1280px-Plymouth_Barbican_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org